  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This Figshare dataset shows early but concrete reuse: it has one documented downstream mention in Europe PMC, while the citation record in OpenAlex remains at zero. The item is openly available through Figshare and appears in two open repository instances, but the usage record is still very small, with only a few views.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">How to edit a manuscript on GitHub with Manubot is a 2019 open dataset by David Slochower and Daniel Himmelstein that supports the Manubot workflow for automated scholarly publishing. Its subject profile points clearly to software, open-source tools, documentation, and web-based manuscript editing, matching the dataset\u2019s role as a supporting media asset rather than a conventional research article.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest signal in the record is reuse rather than citation. Europe PMC records one downstream biomedical article mention, indicating that the dataset has been referenced in later scholarly communication. That is modest in scale, but it is a meaningful sign that the item has been taken up beyond its host repository.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Formal citation evidence is currently absent in the indexed sources available here: OpenAlex reports zero citations, and scite has no citation events recorded for this DOI. The record therefore suggests limited scholarly traceability so far, even though the work is clearly part of an open, citable publishing ecosystem.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Usage and access indicators are also sparse. Figshare reports three views and no downloads, which points to low measured traffic rather than broad or sustained attention. OpenAIRE finds two open instances of the dataset, confirming that the item is discoverable and openly accessible in the repository landscape.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the evidence supports a narrative of small-scale but real scholarly reuse for a practical, method-oriented resource. The dataset\u2019s impact is visible primarily through a documented reuse in the literature, while broader reach signals remain limited in the current record.</p>",
